! Temporary Notes
I use two placeholders for NPs, because I need comments for what these should read.

REF stands for the object or event or whatever that is/happens at some directional offset.

ORIG refers to the end of the previous stage of the imaginary journey (as per CLL), or else the speaker if there is no such stage.

! Proposed Definitions And Examples


!! Proposed Definition of ''be'a''

;__be'a__ (FAhA1): North. Indicates that REF is to the north of ORIG. When tagging a sumti, the sumti indicates something which REF is north of.
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''be'a'' Usage

!! Proposed Definition of ''du'a''

;__du'a__ (FAhA1): East. Indicates that REF is to the east of ORIG. When tagging a sumti, the sumti indicates something which REF is east of.
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''du'a'' Usage

!! Proposed Definition of ''ne'u''

;__ne'u__ (FAhA1): South. Indicates that REF is to the south of ORIG. When tagging a sumti, the sumti indicates something which REF is south of.
